 42.\tab FOCAL-8\par
\par
\tab In 1971 DEC\sub 14\nosupersub  released another edition of PDP-8\sub 99\nosupersub  FOCAL\sub 38\nosupersub  beyond \tab FOCAL, 1969\sub 40\nosupersub ; many users assumed the purpose was to improve the \tab product.  However, upon closer examination, there are many issues \tab that contradict this:\par
\par
\tab a) Support was dropped for the PDP-5\sub 99\nosupersub  and PDP-8/S\sub 99\nosupersub .\par
\par
\tab b) The FOCAL-8 release dropped support for all \ul Family of 8\ulnone\sub 35\nosupersub\par
\tab    machines prior to the OMNIBUS\sub 99\nosupersub  models.\par
\par
\tab    Note: A binary overlay file for FOCAL-8 was sold by DEC\sub 14\nosupersub  that \tab    (partially) restores the former support found in FOCAL,\par
\tab    1969\sub 40\nosupersub ; even with this (extra cost) optional overlay, support\par
\tab    does not exist for the PDP-5\sub 99\nosupersub  and PDP-8/S\sub 99\nosupersub .\par
\par
\tab c) The optional initial dialogue file was dropped; as such, there \tab    is no way to configure the trigonometric functions.\par
\par
\tab d) While nominally FOCAL-8 is only for Omnibus\sub 99\nosupersub  machines (and\par
\tab    the VT78\sub 99\nosupersub ), no actual usage of the (minimal) advanced\par
\tab    features of the newer models exists within the program.  It is\par
\tab    surmised that DEC\sub 14\nosupersub  marketing was determined to drop support\par
\tab    for pre-OMNIBUS\sub 99\nosupersub  machines, even if this consideration was\par
\tab    merely an invention of marketing involving no actual\par
\tab    programming changes.  See b) above.\par
\par
\tab e) The aforementioned minor bug fix for the "for" command coding \tab    is present; however, due to all of the changes made, binary\par
\tab    compatibility\sub 3\nosupersub  with the cumualtive works of the FOCAL, 1969\sub 40\nosupersub  \tab  \par
\tab    user community is lost.\par
\par
\tab    Note: While including the "for" command bug fix coding (as\par
\tab    implemented in FOCAL-8) breaks binary compatibility\sub 3\nosupersub  with\par
\tab    FOCAL, 1969\sub 40\nosupersub , P?S/8 FOCAL\sub 99\nosupersub  includes alternate coding of\par
\tab    the same program fix that maintains binary compatibility\sub 3\nosupersub .\tab    \tab    This comes at the cost of loss of support for the PDP-5\sub 99\nosupersub  and\par
\tab    PDP-8/S\sub 99\nosupersub ; however, this is irrelevant as P?S/8\sub 99\nosupersub  is only\par
\tab    supported on \ul Family of 8\ulnone\sub 35\nosupersub  models.\par
\par
\par
\tab It is surmised that DEC\sub 14\nosupersub  named this product "FOCAL-8" to confuse\par
\tab the customer base, as this is the name used on the FOCAL, 1969\sub 40\nosupersub\par
\tab user manual; the consequence is that many users assumed that\par
\tab FOCAL-8 was a total replacement for FOCAL, 1969\sub 40\nosupersub .  Fortunately, \tab some users realized the products are substantially different; as \tab a result, FOCAL-8 is often referred to as FOCAL-71\sub 41\nosupersub  to \tab distinguish between the two releases.\par
\par
