\tab 3) DEC management tasked the staff with implementing coding to\par
\tab    sabotage attempts to use various DEC products on the competing\par
\tab    DCC-112 and DCC-112H models from Digital Controls Corporation.\par
\par
\tab    When it was determined that this could put DEC at risk for a\par
\tab    lawsuit (they would likely lose), this coding was removed from\par
\tab    OS/8; various surviving OS/8 source files mention the removal\par
\tab    of the DCC code, etc.\par
\par
\tab 4) Likely out of sheer incompetence, the analogous sabotage\par
 \tab    coding was never removed from FOCAL-71.\par
\par
